{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Arrows:</b> He likened the words coming from his mouth to sharpened arrows; so they kill." "<b>With coals:</b> For the arrows in their flight heat up in the air like coals of broom. Now the sense is that this poet — whether he speaks of himself or it is prophecy concerning Israel — is in exile and weeps, for he is a man of truth and dwells in his exile among the nations, and not only that, but there are some among them who speak lies about him and inform against him, so that he be killed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 120, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:06.257897322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}